Fundamental Good Practice in Dimensional Metrology — Flack and Hannaford (@met-dimensional: 0, is #book, #part-of @met-sources) { r_5XRAV7WQWR6CTM94WM04G0Z647
D. R. Flack and J. Hannaford. Fundamental Good Practice in Dimensional Metrology. NPL Measurement Good Practice Guide 80, 2006. English.

[Publisher’s repository entry](https://eprintspublications.npl.co.uk/3360/) · [PDF](https://eprintspublications.npl.co.uk/3360/1/mgpg80.pdf) · [NPL guide page](https://www.npl.co.uk/resources/gpgs/dimensional-metrology-guide).

Read the whole guide while beginning dimensional measurement: length references, traceability, uncertainty, environmental and geometric effects, comparison with specification, and optical methods. Later return to its error-source and technique discussions when writing a measurement procedure. Its introductory scope should lead to an instrument-specific calibration procedure and the current drawing convention in practical work.

The repository identifies the 2006 guide; the NPL landing page also carries a later web publication date. Preserve the edition actually used and its copyright notice; free download is not taken as unrestricted adaptation. Official metadata and contents checked on 28 October 2026. No PDF is bundled.

**Return:** [Measurement and metrology sources — books, guides, and research](../Sources.lingua#r_6H584EJ2Z9D11PG89Y21Y8T1A3).
